<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  CRA-373 Quadruped Robot URDF (Isaac Sim Version)
  Generated: 2026-08-11
  
  Coordinate: Z-up (Isaac Sim / USD standard)
  All mesh transforms baked into STL vertices
  Mesh unit: meters (scale="1 1 1")
  Path: ASCII only, no special characters

  [sim] 2026-09-15 modifications for Isaac Lab / RL training. Search "[sim]" for the list.
  1. Joint velocity limit 209.44 -> 20.944 rad/s on all 12 revolute joints.
     The actuator model gives the joint (output-side) no-load speed as 200 rpm = 20.944 rad/s
     (XB42MCfg.max_velocity). The old value is 209.44 rad/s = 2000 rpm, exactly 10x that, so it
     is a decimal slip rather than a gear-ratio confusion (the reducer is 1:9, not 1:10).
     Isaac Lab writes this to PhysX as velocity_limit_sim, so the error let the joints spin ten
     times faster than the real actuator can.
  2. FR_hip / FL_hip inertial block mirrored in y.
     The front hip MESH is the rear hip mirrored about the x-z plane (mesh centre y -0.0607 vs
     +0.0607), but the inertial block was copied from the rear unchanged, putting 1.45 kg of
     hip mass 0.118 m away from its own geometry on both front legs. com y and the ixy / iyz
     products are now mirrored to match.
  3. Foot inertial origin moved from the link frame origin to the foot geometry.
     The foot link frame sits at the calf joint + (0, 0.154173, 0), while the baked foot mesh
     sits at (+-0.0145, -0.2949, -0.1487) in that frame, i.e. 0.33 m away. The 0.05 kg foot mass
     was therefore placed near the knee instead of at the toe, adding ~0.0054 kg m^2 of phantom
     inertia about the knee (the calf's own ixx is only 0.0043). The inertia tensor is now the
     solid-box estimate for the 20 x 40 x 28.5 mm pad instead of the 1e-4 placeholder.

  4. Collision geometry now points at meshes/collision/, the precomputed convex hulls written
     by scripts/make_collision_meshes.py (530,757 triangles -> 8,152 over the 17 links).
     The importer is configured with collider_type=convex_hull, so PhysX reduced each mesh to
     its hull anyway; precomputing it means the hull is not re-cooked from 539k vertices on
     every load. The collision shape is unchanged. <visual> still uses the full-resolution
     meshes, so the robot still looks like the CAD export.

  NOT changed on purpose:
  - Joint <dynamics>: absent, so damping = friction = 0. Joint friction is modelled once inside
    cra373/actuator/XB42M.py (Coulomb 0.67 Nm); do not also add it here.
  - effort="60.0": XB42M is an explicit actuator, so Isaac sets effort_limit_sim = 1e9 and the
    real torque ceiling is the T-N curve inside XB42MActuator.compute().
  - Masses and inertia magnitudes: 68.16 kg total is confirmed by the robot owner.
-->
<robot name="CRA_373">

  <material name="body_color">  <color rgba="0.50 0.60 0.70 1.0"/> </material>
  <material name="hip_color">   <color rgba="0.80 0.30 0.30 1.0"/> </material>
  <material name="thigh_color"> <color rgba="0.30 0.80 0.30 1.0"/> </material>
  <material name="calf_color">  <color rgba="0.30 0.30 0.80 1.0"/> </material>
  <material name="foot_color">  <color rgba="0.10 0.10 0.10 1.0"/> </material>

  <!-- ==================== BASE LINK ==================== -->
  <link name="base_link">
    <inertial>
      <!-- [sim] com x 0.016986 -> 0, and the ixy / ixz products -> 0.
           The body is left-right symmetric: the base mesh bounding box is centred at x = 0.000
           and the four hip joints sit at x = +-0.081. A centre of mass 17 mm off that centreline
           contradicts the geometry, and on 44.8 kg it is a standing lateral moment the policy
           has to fight every step. Measured on the policy trained with the offset: commanded
           straight ahead at 2 m/s the robot slid 1.32 m sideways over 17 m.
           For a body symmetric about the x = 0 plane the integrals for ixy and ixz vanish too,
           so those are zeroed; iyz is unaffected by that symmetry and is left alone. -->
      <origin xyz="0.0 -0.203646 -0.005118" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="44.830903"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.727300" ixy="0.0" ixz="0.0"
               iyy="0.350700" iyz="0.022770" izz="0.952300"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="meshes/base_link.stl"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="body_color"/>
    </visual>
    <collision>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="meshes/collision/base_link.stl"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>

  <!-- ==================== RR LEG (Right Rear) ==================== -->
  <link name="RR_hip">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="0.020377 0.059012 0.000393" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="1.454366"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.002957" ixy="-0.000229" ixz="0.000003"
               iyy="0.001744" iyz="-0.000001" izz="0.002087"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry><mesh filename="meshes/RR_hip.stl"/></geometry>
      <material name="hip_color"/>
    </visual>
